WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.409 --> 00:00:14.290
[MUSIC]

2
00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:16.367
From a Watchlist in the monitor tab,

3
00:00:16.367 --> 00:00:20.863
click the underlying symbol you wish to
create your option straddle trade for.

4
00:00:20.863 --> 00:00:23.633
So long as your tabs are part
of the same windows group,

5
00:00:23.633 --> 00:00:26.355
the underlying will appear
in the order entry panel.

6
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:29.330
To the right of the order entry panel,

7
00:00:29.330 --> 00:00:31.860
select Strategy Builder
from the drop-down menu.

8
00:00:33.110 --> 00:00:38.620
To the lower left of the Strategy Builder
window, ensure the on button is active.

9
00:00:38.620 --> 00:00:40.990
If not, just click it to activate.

10
00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:46.590
Above, you will see the option chain
window populate, with calls to the left

11
00:00:46.590 --> 00:00:50.620
and puts to the right of the straight
column in the middle of the display.

12
00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:57.210
Use the tabs above the call area to
locate different expiration dates.

13
00:00:57.210 --> 00:00:58.562
Above the put display,

14
00:00:58.562 --> 00:01:03.030
use the strikes drop-down to fine-tune
the contracts displayed on screen.

15
00:01:04.330 --> 00:01:05.640
You will see the price and

16
00:01:05.640 --> 00:01:09.580
the daily change of the underlying to
the upper right corner of the window.

17
00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:15.220
Strategy Builder has several predefined
option combinations available from

18
00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:18.650
the strategy drop-down menu to
the lower right of the screen.

19
00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:24.203
Select Straddle from the list and
notice the icon shown in the lower part of

20
00:01:24.203 --> 00:01:28.437
the display, instructing you to click
on a leg to display the Straddle.

21
00:01:28.437 --> 00:01:32.566
Notice that when the cursor is placed
above the bid price of a call,

22
00:01:32.566 --> 00:01:36.702
the software automatically
highlights the pertinent element for

23
00:01:36.702 --> 00:01:38.569
the rest of the combination.

24
00:01:38.569 --> 00:01:43.401
For a short straddle, TWS knows that
selling a call requires the sale of a put

25
00:01:43.401 --> 00:01:46.320
at the same strike and expiration.

26
00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.810
Hence, both legs display in red.

27
00:01:50.050 --> 00:01:53.159
Move the cursor above
the ask price on a call and

28
00:01:53.159 --> 00:01:57.320
see the related leg on the put
side also moves to the ask price.

29
00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:02.147
Locate the design strike you want to
build your short straddle for and

30
00:02:02.147 --> 00:02:04.580
click on the bid price of the call.

31
00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:09.440
Note that a straddle combines the same
strike and same expiration column to put.

32
00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:14.240
Both call and put legs move
down to the Strategy Builder.

33
00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:18.610
Note that clicking on the ask price
would have generated the long straddle.

34
00:02:20.040 --> 00:02:22.680
With both legs of the short
straddle in position.

35
00:02:22.680 --> 00:02:27.488
Below the bid/ask column, you will see
the price quote for the combination.

36
00:02:27.488 --> 00:02:32.354
This is the combined price of both legs,
and in the case of the short straddle,

37
00:02:32.354 --> 00:02:33.770
represents a credit.

38
00:02:35.060 --> 00:02:39.256
Use the Order Entry panel at the bottom
of the page to create the order.

39
00:02:39.256 --> 00:02:42.295
Define the quantity of straddle
combinations to trade.

40
00:02:43.535 --> 00:02:45.905
Choose the right order type
from the drop-down menu.

41
00:02:47.245 --> 00:02:51.279
If using a limit price, choose the value
by clicking in the input field or

42
00:02:51.279 --> 00:02:52.875
simply typing in the value.

43
00:02:54.145 --> 00:02:56.989
Select from the time in force
drop-down whether this is a day or

44
00:02:56.989 --> 00:02:58.445
a good-til-canceled order.

45
00:02:59.705 --> 00:03:01.740
Your order is ready to review.

46
00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:04.660
Click the submit button to
generate an order confirmation.

47
00:03:06.030 --> 00:03:08.670
When you have reviewed the details,
click transmit.

48
00:03:09.880 --> 00:03:12.658
The order is sent for
execution at the exchange and

49
00:03:12.658 --> 00:03:16.110
will appear in the activity panel
to the lower left of mosaic.

50
00:03:17.340 --> 00:03:20.257
To pause or interact with an active order,

51
00:03:20.257 --> 00:03:24.562
click on it in the activity panel and
make the relevant choice.

52
00:03:24.562 --> 00:03:27.896
[MUSIC]